[node name="Marble" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "MAP 2, MARBLE: the Bentham drawing in white marble, one closed rotunda built on maps/marble/models/marble.glb. The GROUND FLOOR is at y -1.0 and is covered in marble spikes from the tower's foot out to the wall. The running lane is a GALLERY WALKWAY, an annulus r 46.7..59.55 at y 23.0 whose inner edge is open: no rail, no trough, a 24 m drop onto the spikes. Its outer edge is the wall of cells: seven tiers of barred cells, three below the walkway and four above it (tier bases -1, 7, 15, 23, 31, 39, 47), a wall top at 55, a dome springing at 57.8 and closing at an apex of 84.8. The model ships its own collision, so this scene adds no geometry: only the tower, the two lethal volumes, the light and the markers.

A prisoner runs one 340 deg lap at r 52 from 5 deg to the portal at 345 deg. THE LANE IS BARE (Ryan, 2026-09-22: \"for the marble level, can you just get rid of all the elements on the ring? just so it looks good for screenshots and trailers and stuff\"): the obstacle course -- 71 placed instances, columns, broken columns, arches, spike patches and strips, pads, the orbs -- came off, and nothing stands on the 340 deg run now but the portal at the finish. The bars at 353 deg stayed, behind the finish and out of every shot of the lane, because the bake and the harness proved them structural rather than scenery: see the Bars node. The models the course used are still in maps/marble/models/; only this scene changed. Off the walkway there is nothing to stand on until the spikes, and SpikeFloor kills before a body reaches them; KillBox below the ground floor catches anything that fell through the world.

The light is the Oculus node's: one shadowed spot at the oculus whose cone lights the whole room (nothing comes through the roof), the same cone drawn as fanned vanes with dust over the tower, and a low colour ambient."

[node name="Environment" type="Node3D" parent="."]

[node name="WorldEnvironment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="Environment"]
environment = SubResource("Env")

[node name="Oculus" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The room's ONE light. Sun: a shadowed SpotLight3D at the oculus (y 78.5) pointing straight down, half-angle 62 deg so its cone covers the whole lane (outer edge 47 deg) and the cell wall up to y 47, soft angular falloff (4) and no distance falloff (daylight through a hole), so the lane is lit and every placed object throws a shadow from the oculus; Beam: six crossed vanes fanned at the same 62 deg, their glow the spot's own angular falloff with a bright 28 deg core and a faint skirt to the edge, so a cone of light is seen coming down over the tower; Motes: the dust inside that cone. Nothing comes through the roof."

